::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q01::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.SYS.1; MLA.A2.SYS.2
Question:
Solve the system y=x+2 and y=6.
{
=A. x\=4#Correct. Substitute y=6 into 6=x+2.
~B. x\=2#This uses the intercept only.
~C. x\=6#This is the y-value, not x.
~D. x\=8#This adds instead of subtracting.
}

::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q02::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6
Question:
How does y=(x-3)² transform y=x²?
{
~A. Left 3#The sign inside parentheses is interpreted oppositely.
=B. Right 3#Correct. x-3 shifts the graph right 3 units.
~C. Up 3#There is no outside +3.
~D. Down 3#There is no outside -3.
}

::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q03::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.7; MLA.A2.FN.8
Question:
If f(x)=x+1 and g(x)=4x, what is f(g(2))?
{
~A. 8#This stops after g(2).
~B. 7#This applies functions in the wrong way.
=C. 9#Correct. g(2)=8 and f(8)=9.
~D. 12#This multiplies after adding.
}

::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q04::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.9; MLA.A2.FN.10
Question:
Find the inverse of f(x)=x-5.
{
~A. f⁻¹(x)\=x-5#This repeats the original.
~B. f⁻¹(x)\=5x#This does not undo subtracting 5.
~C. f⁻¹(x)\=1/(x-5)#Inverse notation is not reciprocal.
=D. f⁻¹(x)\=x+5#Correct. Add 5 to undo subtracting 5.
}

::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q05::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.3; MLA.A2.FN.11; MLA.A2.FN.12
Question:
Which solution is viable if a time model gives t=-4 and t=9?
{
=A. t\=9 only#Correct. Negative time is not viable.
~B. t\=-4 only#Negative time is not viable.
~C. Both values#One value violates the context.
~D. Neither value#The positive time is viable.
}

